IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- the provisions a person bringing or answering a claim
-- meets: Part 6 whole (discriminatory, coercive and misleading conduct: ss 104 to 115), the claims machinery of Part 13
-- Division 1 (asking for a prosecution and the limitation period, ss 231, 232), Part 12 (review of decisions,
-- ss 223 to 229), compensation for an inspector's use of power (s 184), what the Act does to civil claims (s 267), no
-- contracting out (s 272) and no levy on workers (s 273), with the tier A and tier F penalties of Schedule 4 cl 2.
--
-- SEAT: the individual the law is applied to: the worker, prospective worker or other person who was punished,
-- pressured or misled for a safety reason; the injured worker or family member who wants a prosecution brought; the
-- worker affected by an inspector's decision; the worker charged for safety. The questions are in whs-claims-seat.l4,
-- which imports this module and restates no rule.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 16, compilation date 1 July 2024, includes amendments up to Act No. 120, 2023 (register id
-- C2024C00243), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2011A00137.txt.
--
-- PENALTIES ARE THE SCHEDULE 4 FIGURES BEFORE INDEXATION. Schedule 4 cl 4 indexes them each 1 July from 2024;
-- ../baseline-2026-10/whs-penalty-indexation.l4 indexes them, and cannot be imported from this folder.
--
-- This encoding sits beside baseline-2026-10, which it leaves untouched. That encoding's worker seat already answers
-- the short form of ss 104 to 106, 112, 113(1) and 115(a); this one encodes Part 6 whole and the machinery around it.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults and the 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05
-- rulings on negatives (JUST FALSE where the text says no, NOTHING where it does not answer). No pipeline, no coverage
-- table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Work Health and Safety Act 2011 -- claims`

§§ `Dates`

-- The only module that imports daydate. "Within N days after the day" excludes that day (Acts Interpretation Act 1901
-- s 36(1), not deposited here; read as the plain words), so the last day is the day plus N.

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`days after` `the day` `days` MEANS `the day` PLUS `days`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`months after` `the day` `months` MEANS `add months` `the day` `months`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`years after` `the day` `years` MEANS `add years` `the day` `years`

GIVEN `first` IS A DATE, `second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from` `first` `to` `second` MEANS Day `second` MINUS Day `first`

GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` `d` `m` `y` MEANS Date `d` `m` `y`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` `a` `b` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` `a` `b` MEANS IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `Part 6 Division 1 -- discriminatory, coercive and misleading conduct`

-- s 105(1): "a person engages in discriminatory conduct if: (a) the person: (i) dismisses a worker; or (ii) terminates a
-- contract for services with a worker; or (iii) puts a worker to his or her detriment in the engagement of the worker;
-- or (iv) alters the position of a worker to the worker's detriment; or (b) the person: (i) refuses or fails to offer to
-- engage a prospective worker; or (ii) treats a prospective worker less favourably than another prospective worker would
-- be treated in offering terms of engagement; or (c) the person terminates a commercial arrangement with another person;
-- or (d) the person refuses or fails to enter into a commercial arrangement with another person."
DECLARE `What they did` IS ONE OF
    `dismissed me (s 105(1)(a)(i))`
    `ended my contract for services (s 105(1)(a)(ii))`
    `put me to my detriment in my engagement (s 105(1)(a)(iii))`
    `altered my position to my detriment (s 105(1)(a)(iv))`
    `did not offer to engage me (s 105(1)(b)(i))`
    `offered me worse terms of engagement than another prospective worker (s 105(1)(b)(ii))`
    `ended a commercial arrangement with me (s 105(1)(c))`
    `refused or failed to enter into a commercial arrangement with me (s 105(1)(d))`
    `none of these`

-- s 105(2): "a person also engages in discriminatory conduct if the person organises to take any action referred to in
-- subsection (1) or threatens to organise or take that action." Organising or threatening one of the heads is the same
-- answer as doing it, so it is folded into the choice ("did, or organised, or threatened to do").

-- s 105 is a definition introduced by "if": outside its heads the answer is JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `what they did` IS A `What they did`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 -- it is discriminatory conduct` `what they did` MEANS
    IF `what they did` EQUALS `none of these` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 106: conduct "is engaged in for a prohibited reason if it is engaged in because the worker or prospective worker or
-- the person referred to in section 105(1)(c) or (d) (as the case requires): (a) is, has been or proposes to be a health
-- and safety representative or a member of a health and safety committee; or (b) undertakes ... another role under this
-- Act; or (c) exercises a power or performs a function ... as a health and safety representative or as a member of a
-- health and safety committee; or (d) exercises ... a power under this Act ...; or (e) performs ... a function under this
-- Act ...; or (f) refrains from ... exercising a power or performing a function under this Act ...; or (g) assists ... or
-- gives ... any information to any person exercising a power or performing a function under this Act; or (h) raises or
-- has raised or proposes to raise an issue or concern about work health and safety with: (i) the person conducting a
-- business or undertaking; or (ii) an inspector; or (iii) a WHS entry permit holder; or (iv) a health and safety
-- representative; or (v) a member of a health and safety committee; or (vi) another worker; or (vii) any other person
-- who has a duty under this Act in relation to the matter; or (viii) any other person exercising a power or performing a
-- function under this Act; or (i) is involved in ... resolving a work health and safety issue under this Act; or (j) is
-- taking action ... to seek compliance by any person with any duty or obligation under this Act."
-- Each paragraph covers the past, the present and a proposal; the inputs say so in their wording.
DECLARE `Why they did it` IS ONE OF
    `I am, was or proposed to be a health and safety representative or committee member (s 106(a))`
    `I took on, or proposed to take on, another role under the Act (s 106(b))`
    `I acted, or proposed to act, as a health and safety representative or committee member (s 106(c))`
    `I exercised, or proposed to exercise, a power under the Act, such as stopping unsafe work (s 106(d))`
    `I performed, or proposed to perform, a function under the Act (s 106(e))`
    `I refrained, or proposed to refrain, from exercising a power or performing a function under the Act (s 106(f))`
    `I assisted, or gave information to, someone exercising a power or function under the Act (s 106(g))`
    `I raised, or proposed to raise, a health or safety issue or concern (s 106(h))`
    `I was involved in resolving a health and safety issue under the Act (s 106(i))`
    `I sought compliance by someone with a duty or obligation under the Act (s 106(j))`
    `another reason`

DECLARE `Whom I raised it with` IS ONE OF
    `the business or undertaking (s 106(h)(i))`
    `an inspector (s 106(h)(ii))`
    `a WHS entry permit holder (s 106(h)(iii))`
    `a health and safety representative (s 106(h)(iv))`
    `a health and safety committee member (s 106(h)(v))`
    `another worker (s 106(h)(vi))`
    `another person with a duty under the Act about the matter (s 106(h)(vii))`
    `another person exercising a power or performing a function under the Act (s 106(h)(viii))`
    `someone else, such as the media, a family member or a friend`
    `I did not raise an issue`

-- s 106 is a definition introduced by "if", and paragraph (h) closes its list of persons: outside it, JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `why they did it` IS A `Why they did it`, `whom I raised it with` IS A `Whom I raised it with`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106 -- it was for a prohibited reason` `why they did it` `whom I raised it with` MEANS
    IF `why they did it` EQUALS `another reason`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `why they did it` EQUALS `I raised, or proposed to raise, a health or safety issue or concern (s 106(h))`
         THEN JUST ((NOT (`whom I raised it with` EQUALS `someone else, such as the media, a family member or a friend`))
                    AND (NOT (`whom I raised it with` EQUALS `I did not raise an issue`)))
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 108(1): "A person must not organise or take, or threaten to organise or take, any action against another person
-- with intent to coerce or induce the other person, or a third person: (a) to exercise or not to exercise a power ...
-- under this Act; or (b) to perform or not to perform a function ... under this Act; or (c) to exercise or not to
-- exercise a power or perform a function ... in a particular way; or (d) to refrain from seeking, or continuing to
-- undertake, a role under this Act." (2): taking action includes not taking a particular action. (3): "a reasonable
-- direction given by an emergency services worker in an emergency is not an action with intent to coerce or induce".
DECLARE `What they tried to make me do` IS ONE OF
    `use, or not use, a power under the Act (s 108(1)(a))`
    `perform, or not perform, a function under the Act (s 108(1)(b))`
    `use a power or perform a function in a particular way (s 108(1)(c))`
    `give up seeking, or stop holding, a role under the Act (s 108(1)(d))`
    `something else`

-- A flat negative ("must not") with a closed list of aims: outside the aims, or for an emergency direction, JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `they took or threatened action against me, or withheld or threatened to withhold it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they meant to coerce or induce` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what they tried to make me do` IS A `What they tried to make me do`
      `it was a reasonable direction by an emergency services worker in an emergency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108 -- it was prohibited coercion or inducement` `they took or threatened action against me, or withheld or threatened to withhold it` `they meant to coerce or induce` `what they tried to make me do` `it was a reasonable direction by an emergency services worker in an emergency` MEANS
    JUST (    `they took or threatened action against me, or withheld or threatened to withhold it`
          AND `they meant to coerce or induce`
          AND (NOT (`what they tried to make me do` EQUALS `something else`))
          AND (NOT `it was a reasonable direction by an emergency services worker in an emergency`))

-- s 109(1): "A person must not knowingly or recklessly make a false or misleading representation to another person
-- about that other person's: (a) rights or obligations under this Act; or (b) ability to initiate, or participate in, a
-- process or proceedings under this Act; or (c) ability to make a complaint or inquiry to a person or body empowered under
-- this Act to seek compliance with this Act." (2): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the person to whom the
-- representation is made would not be expected to rely on it."
DECLARE `What I was misled about` IS ONE OF
    `my rights or obligations under the Act (s 109(1)(a))`
    `whether I can start or take part in a process or proceeding under the Act (s 109(1)(b))`
    `whether I can complain or inquire to someone who enforces the Act (s 109(1)(c))`
    `something else`

GIVEN `it was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they knew, or were reckless` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what I was misled about` IS A `What I was misled about`
      `I would be expected to rely on it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109 -- it was prohibited misrepresentation` `it was false or misleading` `they knew, or were reckless` `what I was misled about` `I would be expected to rely on it` MEANS
    JUST (    `it was false or misleading`
          AND `they knew, or were reckless`
          AND (NOT (`what I was misled about` EQUALS `something else`))
          AND `I would be expected to rely on it`)

-- Schedule 4 cl 2, item 1: "the tier A monetary penalty": an individual $139,000; a body corporate $695,000. Item 6:
-- "the tier F monetary penalty": an individual $7,000; a body corporate $35,000. Before indexation under cl 4.
GIVEN `a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule 4 cl 2 -- the tier A monetary penalty` `a body corporate` MEANS
    IF `a body corporate` THEN 695000 ELSE 139000

GIVEN `a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule 4 cl 2 -- the tier F monetary penalty` `a body corporate` MEANS
    IF `a body corporate` THEN 35000 ELSE 7000

§§ `Part 6 Division 2 -- criminal proceedings`

-- s 104(2): "A person commits an offence under subsection (1) only if the reason referred to in section 106 was the
-- dominant reason for the discriminatory conduct." s 110(2): "The reason alleged ... is presumed to be the dominant reason
-- ... unless the accused proves on the balance of probabilities, that the reason was not the dominant reason" (once the
-- prosecution proves the conduct and the s 106 circumstance and adduces evidence of the prohibited reason, s 110(1)).
GIVEN `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused proved the reason was not the dominant one` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 104(2), 110 -- the dominant-reason element is met` `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` `the accused proved the reason was not the dominant one` MEANS
    JUST (`discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` AND (NOT `the accused proved the reason was not the dominant one`))

DECLARE `Order` IS ONE OF
    `an injunction (s 112(3)(a))`
    `compensation within a specified period (s 112(3)(b))`
    `reinstatement or re-employment, or employment in the position applied for (s 112(3)(c))`
    `any other order the court considers appropriate (s 112(3)(d))`
    `compensation within a specified period, on conviction (s 111(a))`
    `reinstatement or re-employment, or employment in the position applied for, on conviction (s 111(b))`

-- s 111: "If a person is convicted or found guilty of an offence under section 104 or 107, the court may (in addition to
-- imposing a penalty) make either or both of the following orders: (a) ... compensation to the person who was the
-- subject of the discriminatory conduct ...; (b) in relation to a person who was or is an employee or prospective
-- employee, an order that: (i) the person be reinstated or re-employed ... or (ii) the person be employed in the position
-- for which he or she had applied". s 114(2): "If the court makes an order under section 112 ... in relation to conduct
-- referred to in section 112(2)(a) or (b), the court cannot make an order under section 111 ... in relation to the same
-- conduct."
GIVEN `convicted or found guilty under s 104 or 107` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was or am an employee or prospective employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a s 112 order was made about the same conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Order`
`s 111 -- the orders open on conviction` `convicted or found guilty under s 104 or 107` `I was or am an employee or prospective employee` `a s 112 order was made about the same conduct` MEANS
    IF (NOT `convicted or found guilty under s 104 or 107`) OR `a s 112 order was made about the same conduct`
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE IF `I was or am an employee or prospective employee`
         THEN LIST `compensation within a specified period, on conviction (s 111(a))`, `reinstatement or re-employment, or employment in the position applied for, on conviction (s 111(b))`
         ELSE LIST `compensation within a specified period, on conviction (s 111(a))`

§§ `Part 6 Division 3 -- civil proceedings`

-- s 112(2): orders "in relation to a person who has: (a) engaged in discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason; or
-- (b) requested, instructed, induced, encouraged, authorised or assisted another person to engage in discriminatory
-- conduct for a prohibited reason; or (c) contravened section 108."
DECLARE `Their part in it` IS ONE OF
    `they did it themselves (s 112(2)(a))`
    `they requested, instructed, induced, encouraged, authorised or assisted another to do it (s 112(2)(b))`

DECLARE `What I complain of` IS ONE OF
    `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason`
    `coercion or inducement under s 108`
    `misrepresentation under s 109`
    `nothing Part 6 prohibits`

-- s 112(6): "each of the following is an eligible person: (a) a person affected by the contravention; (b) a person
-- authorised as a representative by a person referred to in paragraph (a)."
DECLARE `Who I am in the claim` IS ONE OF
    `the person affected (s 112(6)(a))`
    `a representative authorised by the person affected (s 112(6)(b))`
    `someone else`

-- s 113(1): "A proceeding brought under section 112 must be commenced not more than 1 year after the date on which the
-- applicant knew or ought to have known that the cause of action accrued."
GIVEN `the day I knew, or ought to have known` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 113(1) -- the last day to start` `the day I knew, or ought to have known` MEANS
    `years after` `the day I knew, or ought to have known` 1

-- s 115: "A person cannot: (a) commence a proceeding under Division 3 of this Part if the person has commenced a
-- proceeding or made an application or complaint in relation to the same matter under a law of the Commonwealth or a
-- State and that proceeding, application or complaint has not been withdrawn; or (b) recover any compensation under
-- Division 3 of this Part if the person has received compensation for the matter under a law of the Commonwealth or a
-- State; or (c) commence or continue an application under Division 3 of this Part if the person has failed in a
-- proceeding, application or complaint in relation to the same matter under a law of the Commonwealth or a State, other
-- than a proceeding, application or complaint relating to workers' compensation."
DECLARE `Can I start a s 112 proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I may apply to a court for an order under s 112 (s 112(1)), in the Federal Court, the Federal Circuit and Family Court (Division 2) or a Supreme Court (s 273A)`
    `no: nothing I complain of is conduct s 112(2) reaches (misrepresentation under s 109 is an offence only)`
    `no: I am not an eligible person (s 112(6))`
    `no: it is more than 1 year after I knew or ought to have known of the claim (s 113(1))`
    `no: I have another proceeding, application or complaint about the same matter that is not withdrawn (s 115(a))`
    `no: I failed in another proceeding, application or complaint about the same matter, not a workers' compensation one (s 115(c))`

GIVEN `what I complain of` IS A `What I complain of`
      `who I am in the claim` IS A `Who I am in the claim`
      `the day I knew, or ought to have known` IS A DATE
      `the day I would start` IS A DATE
      `I have another live claim about the same matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I failed in another claim about the same matter, not workers' compensation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Can I start a s 112 proceeding`
`ss 112, 113(1), 115(a), (c) -- whether I can start` `what I complain of` `who I am in the claim` `the day I knew, or ought to have known` `the day I would start` `I have another live claim about the same matter` `I failed in another claim about the same matter, not workers' compensation` MEANS
    IF (`what I complain of` EQUALS `misrepresentation under s 109`) OR (`what I complain of` EQUALS `nothing Part 6 prohibits`)
    THEN `no: nothing I complain of is conduct s 112(2) reaches (misrepresentation under s 109 is an offence only)`
    ELSE IF `who I am in the claim` EQUALS `someone else`
         THEN `no: I am not an eligible person (s 112(6))`
         ELSE IF `the day I would start` GREATER THAN `s 113(1) -- the last day to start` `the day I knew, or ought to have known`
              THEN `no: it is more than 1 year after I knew or ought to have known of the claim (s 113(1))`
              ELSE IF `I have another live claim about the same matter`
                   THEN `no: I have another proceeding, application or complaint about the same matter that is not withdrawn (s 115(a))`
                   ELSE IF `I failed in another claim about the same matter, not workers' compensation`
                        THEN `no: I failed in another proceeding, application or complaint about the same matter, not a workers' compensation one (s 115(c))`
                        ELSE `yes: I may apply to a court for an order under s 112 (s 112(1)), in the Federal Court, the Federal Circuit and Family Court (Division 2) or a Supreme Court (s 273A)`

-- s 112(4): discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason may be found "only if a reason referred to in section 106 was
-- a substantial reason for the conduct". s 113(2): the alleged reason "is presumed to be a substantial reason for that
-- conduct unless the defendant proves, on the balance of probabilities, that the reason was not a substantial reason".
-- s 113(3): "It is a defence ... in relation to conduct referred to in section 112(2)(a) or (b) if the defendant proves
-- that: (a) the conduct was reasonable in the circumstances; and (b) a substantial reason for the conduct was to comply
-- with the requirements of this Act or a corresponding WHS law." Neither applies to s 108 coercion.
-- s 112(3)(b): compensation only "in the case of conduct referred to in subsection (2)(a) or (b)"; (c): reinstatement or
-- employment only "in the case of conduct referred to in subsection (2)(a) in relation to a worker who was or is an
-- employee or prospective employee". s 114(3): after a s 111 order, "the court cannot make an order under section 112
-- ... in relation to conduct referred to in section 112(2)(a) or (b) that is the same conduct". s 115(b): no compensation
-- recovered under Division 3 after compensation "for the matter under a law of the Commonwealth or a State".
GIVEN `what I complain of` IS A `What I complain of`
      `their part in it` IS A `Their part in it`
      `they proved the safety reason was not a substantial reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they proved their conduct was reasonable and substantially to comply with a WHS law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was or am an employee or prospective employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a s 111 order was made about the same conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have received compensation for the matter under another law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Order`
`s 112(3) -- the orders the court may make` `what I complain of` `their part in it` `they proved the safety reason was not a substantial reason` `they proved their conduct was reasonable and substantially to comply with a WHS law` `I was or am an employee or prospective employee` `a s 111 order was made about the same conduct` `I have received compensation for the matter under another law` MEANS
    IF `what I complain of` EQUALS `coercion or inducement under s 108`
    THEN LIST `an injunction (s 112(3)(a))`, `any other order the court considers appropriate (s 112(3)(d))`
    ELSE IF NOT (`what I complain of` EQUALS `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason`)
         THEN EMPTY
         ELSE IF `they proved the safety reason was not a substantial reason` OR `they proved their conduct was reasonable and substantially to comply with a WHS law` OR `a s 111 order was made about the same conduct`
              THEN EMPTY
              ELSE concat (LIST (LIST `injunction`), `compensation`, `reinstatement`, (LIST `any other order the court considers appropriate (s 112(3)(d))`))
    WHERE
        `injunction` MEANS `an injunction (s 112(3)(a))`
        `compensation` MEANS
            IF `I have received compensation for the matter under another law`
            THEN EMPTY
            ELSE LIST `compensation within a specified period (s 112(3)(b))`
        `reinstatement` MEANS
            IF (`their part in it` EQUALS `they did it themselves (s 112(2)(a))`) AND `I was or am an employee or prospective employee`
            THEN LIST `reinstatement or re-employment, or employment in the position applied for (s 112(3)(c))`
            ELSE EMPTY

§§ `Part 13 Division 1 -- asking for a prosecution, and the limitation period`

-- s 231(1): applies if a person "(i) reasonably considers that the occurrence of an act, matter or thing constitutes a
-- Category 1 offence, a Category 2 offence or an offence against subsection 30A(1) (industrial manslaughter); or (ii)
-- reasonably considers, from a coronial report or the proceedings at a coronial inquiry or inquest, that [such an offence]
-- has been committed; and (b) no prosecution for the offence has been brought." (1A): "The person may make a written
-- request to the regulator that a prosecution be brought." (1B): "The request may only be made: (a) if subsection
-- (1)(a)(i) applies -- at least 6 months but not more than 18 months after the act, matter or thing occurs; or (b) if
-- subsection (1)(a)(ii) applies -- within 6 months after the report is made or the inquiry or inquest ends."
DECLARE `The offence I consider was committed` IS ONE OF
    `industrial manslaughter (s 30A(1))`
    `a Category 1 offence (s 31)`
    `a Category 2 offence (s 32)`
    `a Category 3 offence (s 33)`
    `another offence against the Act`

DECLARE `What I base it on` IS ONE OF
    `what happened (s 231(1)(a)(i))`
    `a coronial report, inquiry or inquest (s 231(1)(a)(ii))`

DECLARE `Request window` HAS
    `the first day` IS A DATE
    `the last day` IS A DATE

-- "At least 6 months ... after" the occurrence: the first day is 6 months on; "not more than 18 months after": the last
-- day is 18 months on. "Within 6 months after the report is made": from the day of the report to 6 months on.
GIVEN `what I base it on` IS A `What I base it on`, `the day it happened, or the report or inquest ended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Request window`
`s 231(1B) -- the window` `what I base it on` `the day it happened, or the report or inquest ended` MEANS
    IF `what I base it on` EQUALS `what happened (s 231(1)(a)(i))`
    THEN `Request window` WITH
             `the first day` IS `months after` `the day it happened, or the report or inquest ended` 6
             `the last day`  IS `months after` `the day it happened, or the report or inquest ended` 18
    ELSE `Request window` WITH
             `the first day` IS `the day it happened, or the report or inquest ended`
             `the last day`  IS `months after` `the day it happened, or the report or inquest ended` 6

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `The offence I consider was committed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 231(1) -- an offence a request can be about` `the offence` MEANS
       `the offence` EQUALS `industrial manslaughter (s 30A(1))`
    OR `the offence` EQUALS `a Category 1 offence (s 31)`
    OR `the offence` EQUALS `a Category 2 offence (s 32)`

-- "This section applies if ... and"; "may only be made": outside them, JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `The offence I consider was committed`
      `I reasonably consider it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a prosecution has been brought` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what I base it on` IS A `What I base it on`
      `the day it happened, or the report or inquest ended` IS A DATE
      `the day I would ask` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(1), (1A), (1B) -- I may ask` `the offence` `I reasonably consider it` `a prosecution has been brought` `what I base it on` `the day it happened, or the report or inquest ended` `the day I would ask` MEANS
    JUST (    `s 231(1) -- an offence a request can be about` `the offence`
          AND `I reasonably consider it`
          AND (NOT `a prosecution has been brought`)
          AND `the day I would ask` AT LEAST `the window`'s `the first day`
          AND `the day I would ask` AT MOST `the window`'s `the last day`)
    WHERE
        `the window` MEANS `s 231(1B) -- the window` `what I base it on` `the day it happened, or the report or inquest ended`

-- s 231(2): "Within 3 months after the regulator receives a request the regulator must: (a) advise the person (in
-- writing): (i) whether the investigation is complete; and (ii) if the investigation is complete, whether a prosecution
-- has been or will be brought or give reasons why a prosecution will not be brought". A regulative rule on Comcare, the
-- regulator (s 4), counted in days from the day it received the request.
DECLARE `Request party` IS ONE OF `Comcare`
DECLARE `Request action` IS ONE OF
    `advise the person in writing (s 231(2)(a))`
    `refer the matter to the Director of Public Prosecutions (s 231(3)(b))`

GIVEN `days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Request party` `Request action`
`s 231(2) -- Comcare must advise me` `days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `Comcare`
    MUST `advise the person in writing (s 231(2)(a))`
    WITHIN `days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `Comcare` BECAUSE "s 231(2): no written advice within 3 months after the regulator received the request"

GIVEN `the day Comcare received my request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 231(2) -- the last day for the advice` `the day Comcare received my request` MEANS
    `months after` `the day Comcare received my request` 3

-- Runs the duty over what happened. An answer given on `the day asked about` stands for "had it advised today": if that
-- would not fulfil the duty, it is late. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE matches FULFILLED only.
GIVEN `the day Comcare received my request` IS A DATE
      `it has advised me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it advised me` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 231(2) -- the duty was kept, or can still be` `the day Comcare received my request` `it has advised me` `the day it advised me` `the day asked about` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 231(2) -- Comcare must advise me` `days allowed`) 0 `the events`
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        `days allowed` MEANS `days from` `the day Comcare received my request` `to` (`s 231(2) -- the last day for the advice` `the day Comcare received my request`)
        `the day of the advice` MEANS IF `it has advised me` THEN `the day it advised me` ELSE `the day asked about`
        `the events` MEANS LIST (EVENT `Comcare` `advise the person in writing (s 231(2)(a))` (`days from` `the day Comcare received my request` `to` `the day of the advice`))

-- s 231(3): if Comcare advises that "a prosecution for a Category 1 offence, a Category 2 offence or an offence against
-- subsection 30A(1) ... will not be brought, the regulator must: (a) advise the person that the person may ask the
-- regulator to refer the matter to the Director of Public Prosecutions for consideration; and (b) if the person makes a
-- written request to the regulator to do so, refer the matter to the Director of Public Prosecutions within 1 month of
-- the request." Where the "if" fails there is no day to give: NOTHING.
GIVEN `Comcare advised that no prosecution will be brought` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I asked in writing for a referral` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I asked for the referral` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 231(3)(b) -- the last day to refer` `Comcare advised that no prosecution will be brought` `I asked in writing for a referral` `the day I asked for the referral` MEANS
    IF `Comcare advised that no prosecution will be brought` AND `I asked in writing for a referral`
    THEN JUST (`months after` `the day I asked for the referral` 1)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 232(1): "Proceedings for an offence against this Act may be brought within the latest of the following periods to
-- occur: (a) within 2 years after the offence first comes to the notice of the regulator; (b) within 1 year after a
-- coronial report was made or a coronial inquiry or inquest ended, or an official inquiry ended if it appeared from the
-- report or the proceedings at the inquiry or inquest that an offence had been committed against this Act; (c) if a WHS
-- undertaking has been given in relation to the offence, within 6 months after: (i) the WHS undertaking is contravened;
-- or (ii) it comes to the notice of the regulator that the WHS undertaking has been contravened; or (iii) the regulator
-- has agreed under section 221 to the withdrawal of the WHS undertaking." (2): a Category 1 offence "may be brought after
-- the end of the applicable limitation period ... if fresh evidence relevant to the offence is discovered and the court
-- ... is satisfied that the evidence could not reasonably have been discovered within the relevant limitation period."
-- (2A): industrial manslaughter "may be brought at any time".
DECLARE `Time to prosecute` IS ONE OF
    `at any time (s 232(2A))`
    `at any time on fresh evidence the court accepts (s 232(2))`
    `until` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `The offence I consider was committed`
      `the day it first came to Comcare's notice` IS A DATE
      `an inquiry or inquest showed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the report was made or the inquiry ended` IS A DATE
      `a WHS undertaking was given and later breached or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the breach, its notice to Comcare, or the withdrawal, whichever is latest` IS A DATE
      `the court is satisfied about fresh evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Time to prosecute`
`s 232 -- how long they can be prosecuted` `the offence` `the day it first came to Comcare's notice` `an inquiry or inquest showed an offence` `the day the report was made or the inquiry ended` `a WHS undertaking was given and later breached or withdrawn` `the day of the breach, its notice to Comcare, or the withdrawal, whichever is latest` `the court is satisfied about fresh evidence` MEANS
    IF `the offence` EQUALS `industrial manslaughter (s 30A(1))`
    THEN `at any time (s 232(2A))`
    ELSE IF (`the offence` EQUALS `a Category 1 offence (s 31)`) AND `the court is satisfied about fresh evidence`
         THEN `at any time on fresh evidence the court accepts (s 232(2))`
         ELSE `until` (`the later of` `period (a)` (`the later of` `period (b)` `period (c)`))
    WHERE
        `period (a)` MEANS `years after` `the day it first came to Comcare's notice` 2
        `period (b)` MEANS
            IF `an inquiry or inquest showed an offence`
            THEN `years after` `the day the report was made or the inquiry ended` 1
            ELSE `period (a)`
        `period (c)` MEANS
            IF `a WHS undertaking was given and later breached or withdrawn`
            THEN `months after` `the day of the breach, its notice to Comcare, or the withdrawal, whichever is latest` 6
            ELSE `period (a)`

§§ `Part 12 -- review of decisions`

-- s 223(1), table: the reviewable decisions and, for each, the eligible persons. Item 13 (a prescribed provision of the
-- regulations) is left out: the Regulations' prescriptions are not read here.
DECLARE `The decision` IS ONE OF
    `an inspector's decision on failed work group negotiations (s 54(2), item 1)`
    `an inspector's decision on training a health and safety representative (s 72(6), item 2)`
    `an inspector's decision on a health and safety committee (s 76(6), item 3)`
    `an inspector's decision on review of a provisional improvement notice (s 102, item 4)`
    `forfeiture of a seized thing (s 179, item 5)`
    `a decision on returning a seized thing (s 180, item 6)`
    `an improvement notice (s 191, item 7)`
    `an extension of time to comply with an improvement notice (s 194, item 8)`
    `a prohibition notice (s 195, item 9)`
    `a non-disturbance notice (s 198, item 10)`
    `a subsequent notice (s 201, item 11)`
    `Comcare's decision to vary or cancel a notice (s 207, item 12)`
    `another decision`

DECLARE `My standing` HAS
    `I am a worker whose interests are affected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am the person to whom the notice was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am the person entitled to the seized thing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a health and safety representative for an affected worker` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The table closes the list of eligible persons ("who is eligible to apply ... (the eligible person)"): outside it,
-- JUST FALSE; for a decision the table does not list, the Act does not answer here (item 13 aside): NOTHING.
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision`, `my standing` IS A `My standing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 223 -- I am an eligible person` `the decision` `my standing` MEANS
    IF `the decision` EQUALS `another decision`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (`the decision` EQUALS `forfeiture of a seized thing (s 179, item 5)`) OR (`the decision` EQUALS `a decision on returning a seized thing (s 180, item 6)`)
         THEN JUST (`my standing`'s `I am the person entitled to the seized thing`)
         ELSE IF `the decision` EQUALS `an inspector's decision on training a health and safety representative (s 72(6), item 2)`
              THEN JUST (`my standing`'s `I am a health and safety representative for an affected worker`)
              ELSE IF (`the decision` EQUALS `an inspector's decision on failed work group negotiations (s 54(2), item 1)`) OR (`the decision` EQUALS `an inspector's decision on a health and safety committee (s 76(6), item 3)`)
                   THEN JUST (`my standing`'s `I am a worker whose interests are affected` OR `my standing`'s `I am a health and safety representative for an affected worker`)
                   ELSE JUST (   `my standing`'s `I am a worker whose interests are affected`
                              OR `my standing`'s `I am a health and safety representative for an affected worker`
                              OR `my standing`'s `I am the person to whom the notice was issued`)

-- s 224(1): internal review is for "a reviewable decision, other than a decision made by the regulator or a delegate of
-- the regulator"; s 229(1): external review by the Fair Work Commission of "(a) a reviewable decision made by the
-- regulator; or (b) a decision made, or taken to have been made, on an internal review". Items 5, 6 and 12 are the
-- regulator's decisions (ss 179, 180, 207); the rest are an inspector's.
DECLARE `Where to go` IS ONE OF
    `internal review by Comcare first (s 224), then the Fair Work Commission (s 229(1)(b))`
    `straight to the Fair Work Commission (s 229(1)(a))`
    `no review: I am not an eligible person (s 223)`
    `not answered here: the decision is not in the s 223 table as encoded`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 224(1) -- a decision of the regulator` `the decision` MEANS
       `the decision` EQUALS `forfeiture of a seized thing (s 179, item 5)`
    OR `the decision` EQUALS `a decision on returning a seized thing (s 180, item 6)`
    OR `the decision` EQUALS `Comcare's decision to vary or cancel a notice (s 207, item 12)`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision`, `my standing` IS A `My standing`
GIVETH A `Where to go`
`ss 223, 224, 229 -- where to go` `the decision` `my standing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 223 -- I am an eligible person` `the decision` `my standing`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `not answered here: the decision is not in the s 223 table as encoded`
    WHEN JUST `eligible` THEN
        IF NOT `eligible`
        THEN `no review: I am not an eligible person (s 223)`
        ELSE IF `s 224(1) -- a decision of the regulator` `the decision`
             THEN `straight to the Fair Work Commission (s 229(1)(a))`
             ELSE `internal review by Comcare first (s 224), then the Fair Work Commission (s 229(1)(b))`

-- s 224(1): within "(a) the prescribed time after the day on which the decision first came to the eligible person's
-- notice; or (b) such longer period as the regulator allows." (3): "the prescribed time is: (a) in the case of a decision
-- to issue an improvement notice the period specified in the notice for compliance with the notice or 14 days, whichever
-- is the lesser; and (b) in any other case, 14 days." The notice states "the day by which the person is required to
-- remedy" (s 192(1)(d)); the compliance period is read as running from the day of issue to that day (fork F6).
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision`
      `the day it first came to my notice` IS A DATE
      `the day the improvement notice was issued` IS A DATE
      `the day the improvement notice requires compliance by` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 224 -- the last day to apply for internal review` `the decision` `the day it first came to my notice` `the day the improvement notice was issued` `the day the improvement notice requires compliance by` MEANS
    `days after` `the day it first came to my notice` `the prescribed time`
    WHERE
        `the prescribed time` MEANS
            IF `the decision` EQUALS `an improvement notice (s 191, item 7)`
            THEN `the smaller of` (`days from` `the day the improvement notice was issued` `to` `the day the improvement notice requires compliance by`) 14
            ELSE 14

-- s 226(1): the internal reviewer must decide "within 14 days after the application for internal review is received".
-- (3): "If the internal reviewer seeks further information from the applicant, the 14-day period ceases to run until
-- the applicant provides the information". (4): the time to provide it is "not less than 7 days" (fork F7). (5): "If the
-- applicant does not provide the further information within the required time, the decision is taken to have been
-- confirmed ... at the end of that time." (6): "If the reviewable decision is not varied or set aside within the 14-day
-- period, the decision is taken to have been confirmed".
GIVEN `the day my application was received` IS A DATE
      `the reviewer asked me for more information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it asked` IS A DATE
      `the days it gave me to answer` IS A NUMBER
      `I gave the information in time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I gave it` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 226 -- the day the decision is taken to be confirmed` `the day my application was received` `the reviewer asked me for more information` `the day it asked` `the days it gave me to answer` `I gave the information in time` `the day I gave it` MEANS
    IF NOT `the reviewer asked me for more information`
    THEN `days after` `the day my application was received` 14
    ELSE IF NOT `I gave the information in time`
         THEN `days after` `the day it asked` (`the larger of` `the days it gave me to answer` 7)
         ELSE `days after` `the day my application was received` (14 PLUS (`days from` `the day it asked` `to` `the day I gave it`))

-- s 228(1): "An application for an internal review of a reviewable decision (other than a decision to issue a
-- prohibition notice or a non-disturbance notice) stays the operation of the decision." (2), (3): for those two the
-- reviewer "may stay" it, on its own initiative or on application. (4), (5): on an application, a decision "within 1
-- working day"; if none, "the reviewer is taken to have made a decision to grant a stay".
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision`
      `I applied for a stay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reviewer decided within 1 working day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reviewer granted a stay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 228 -- the decision is stayed` `the decision` `I applied for a stay` `the reviewer decided within 1 working day` `the reviewer granted a stay` MEANS
    IF NOT ((`the decision` EQUALS `a prohibition notice (s 195, item 9)`) OR (`the decision` EQUALS `a non-disturbance notice (s 198, item 10)`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `I applied for a stay` AND (NOT `the reviewer decided within 1 working day`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST `the reviewer granted a stay`

-- s 229(2): "(a) if the decision was to forfeit a thing (including a document), within 28 days after the day on which
-- the decision first came to the applicant's notice; or (b) in the case of any other decision, within 14 days after the
-- day on which the decision first came to the applicant's notice; or (c) if the regulator is required by the external
-- review body to give the eligible person a statement of reasons, within 14 days after the day on which the statement
-- is provided." (c) is read as replacing (a) or (b) when it applies (fork F8).
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision`
      `the day the decision first came to my notice` IS A DATE
      `the Commission required Comcare to give me reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the reasons were given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 229(2) -- the last day to apply to the Fair Work Commission` `the decision` `the day the decision first came to my notice` `the Commission required Comcare to give me reasons` `the day the reasons were given` MEANS
    IF `the Commission required Comcare to give me reasons`
    THEN `days after` `the day the reasons were given` 14
    ELSE IF `the decision` EQUALS `forfeiture of a seized thing (s 179, item 5)`
         THEN `days after` `the day the decision first came to my notice` 28
         ELSE `days after` `the day the decision first came to my notice` 14

§§ `Part 9 Division 4 -- compensation for an inspector's powers`

-- s 184(1): "A person may claim compensation from the Commonwealth if the person incurs loss or expense because of the
-- exercise or purported exercise of a power under Division 3 of this Part" (powers relating to entry, ss 163 to 181).
-- (2): in a proceeding "(a) brought in a court; or (b) for an offence against this Act brought against the person
-- claiming compensation." (3): "The court may order compensation to be paid only if it is satisfied it is just".
GIVEN `I incurred loss or expense` IS A BOOLEAN, `it was because of an inspector's entry, search, seizure or other power under ss 163 to 181` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(1) -- I may claim` `I incurred loss or expense` `it was because of an inspector's entry, search, seizure or other power under ss 163 to 181` MEANS
    JUST (`I incurred loss or expense` AND `it was because of an inspector's entry, search, seizure or other power under ss 163 to 181`)

GIVEN `I may claim` IS A BOOLEAN, `the court is satisfied it is just` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(3) -- the court may order it` `I may claim` `the court is satisfied it is just` MEANS
    JUST (`I may claim` AND `the court is satisfied it is just`)

§§ `Part 13 s 267, Part 14 ss 272, 273 -- civil claims, contracts and charges`

-- s 267: "Except as provided in Part 6 and Part 7 and Division 7 of this Part, nothing in this Act is to be construed as:
-- (a) conferring a right of action in civil proceedings in relation to a contravention of a provision of this Act; or (b)
-- conferring a defence to an action in civil proceedings or otherwise affecting a right of action in civil proceedings".
-- Division 7 proceedings (WHS civil penalty provisions, all in Part 7) "may only be brought by: (a) the regulator; or (b)
-- an inspector" (s 260). So the only civil proceeding the Act gives an individual is Part 6's (s 112).
DECLARE `My civil claim is about` IS ONE OF
    `a breach of a health and safety duty, such as an injury at work`
    `discriminatory or coercive conduct under Part 6`
    `a contravention of a WHS civil penalty provision in Part 7 (entry permits)`
    `another contravention of the Act`

GIVEN `my claim is about` IS A `My civil claim is about`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 267 -- the Act gives me a right of action` `my claim is about` MEANS
    IF `my claim is about` EQUALS `discriminatory or coercive conduct under Part 6`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 272: "A term of any agreement or contract that purports to exclude, limit or modify the operation of this Act or any
-- duty owed under this Act or to transfer to another person any duty owed under this Act is void." For any other term the
-- section is silent: NOTHING.
GIVEN `the term excludes, limits or modifies the Act or a duty under it` IS A BOOLEAN, `the term transfers a duty under the Act to someone else` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272 -- the term is void` `the term excludes, limits or modifies the Act or a duty under it` `the term transfers a duty under the Act to someone else` MEANS
    IF `the term excludes, limits or modifies the Act or a duty under it` OR `the term transfers a duty under the Act to someone else`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 273: "A person conducting a business or undertaking must not impose a levy or charge on a worker, or permit a levy
-- or charge to be imposed on a worker, for anything done, or provided, in relation to work health and safety. Penalty:
-- The tier F monetary penalty." A prohibition with no period of its own: WITHIN 1 stands for the one period the question
-- asks about, so that a trace with no charge ends FULFILLED (fork F10).
DECLARE `Levy party` IS ONE OF `the business or undertaking`
DECLARE `Levy action` IS ONE OF `impose or permit a levy or charge on me for work health and safety`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Levy party` `Levy action`
`s 273 -- the business must not charge me for safety` MEANS
    PARTY `the business or undertaking`
    SHANT `impose or permit a levy or charge on me for work health and safety`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST BREACH BY `the business or undertaking` BECAUSE "s 273: a levy or charge on a worker for work health and safety; tier F monetary penalty"

GIVEN `it happened` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 273 -- the prohibition was kept` `it happened` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 273 -- the business must not charge me for safety` 0 `the events`
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        `the events` MEANS
            IF `it happened`
            THEN LIST (EVENT `the business or undertaking` `impose or permit a levy or charge on me for work health and safety` 0), (WAITUNTIL 2)
            ELSE LIST (WAITUNTIL 2)
